1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:03,169
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,302 --> 00:00:14,014
[Ivy] <i>Thirteen years. I longed for you.</i>

3
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:16,516
<i>And now, Mom? I'm with you again.</i>

4
00:00:16,599 --> 00:00:19,394
<i>But it hurts because</i>
<i>you can't remember me.</i>

5
00:00:19,811 --> 00:00:21,771
[Diego] <i>I'll do everything</i>
<i>to find out the truth.</i>

6
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:23,940
<i>I just want answers to my questions.</i>

7
00:00:24,023 --> 00:00:26,067
<i>So I can freely love Ivy… or Lily.</i>

8
00:00:26,151 --> 00:00:28,778
[Arnaldo] <i>Carlotta, I know Ivy's</i>
<i>hiding something from me.</i>

9
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:30,405
<i>And I swear, I'll find out what it is.</i>

10
00:00:30,488 --> 00:00:32,157
<i>Be honest with me. What's</i>
<i>going on between you and Ivy?</i>

11
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:33,366
<i>-Nothing.</i>
<i>-She's missing!</i>

12
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:35,577
<i>Did you kidnap her</i>
<i>so you could get back at Grandpa?</i>

13
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:37,078
<i>Your grandfather is just using that woman.</i>

14
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:38,830
<i>Right now, she's useful to him.</i>

15
00:00:38,913 --> 00:00:40,457
<i>But he'll eventually get rid of her too.</i>

16
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:42,917
<i>Just like you and your mom!</i>

17
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:44,210
[Julio] <i>My daughter, Emilia.</i>

18
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:48,214
<i>She has been diagnosed</i>
<i>with ovarian cancer, stage 2.</i>

19
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:52,218
<i>I need to step down as</i>
<i>the governor of this province.</i>

20
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:54,637
[Julio] <i>Governor Emilia's successor</i>

21
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:57,640
<i>will be Governor William Alvarez!</i>

22
00:00:57,849 --> 00:00:58,767
[teacher] <i>Ivy?</i>

23
00:00:58,850 --> 00:01:02,187
<i>According to Mrs. Aguas,</i>
<i>Ivy went through a lot.</i>

24
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:04,981
<i>Something to do with</i>
<i>her childhood and her real mom.</i>

25
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:07,442
-[Diego] <i>Hold on. Her real mom?</i>
-[teacher] <i>Yes.</i>

26
00:01:07,525 --> 00:01:09,486
<i>Ivy is Mrs. Aguas' adopted daughter.</i>

27
00:01:09,569 --> 00:01:11,446
[Diego] <i>You don't have to lie anymore.</i>

28
00:01:11,529 --> 00:01:13,782
<i>I already know who Ivy really is.</i>

29
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:15,533
[Julio] <i>I want you to take</i>

30
00:01:15,617 --> 00:01:18,495
<i>all of Emilia's and Raul's belongings,</i>

31
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:20,997
<i>and move them to the old guesthouse</i>

32
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:21,998
<i>at the back of our house.</i>

33
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:26,211
<i>I promise I'll return</i>
<i>to that mansion! I swear it!</i>

34
00:01:26,753 --> 00:01:30,131
[sobbing] <i>Lily. Lily!</i>

35
00:01:30,965 --> 00:01:33,968
[Ivy] <i>Yes. That's me. I'm Lily.</i>
<i>Do you remember me now?</i>

36
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:39,933
Do you remember me now, Mom?
It's me. I'm Lily.

37
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:42,143
[sobbing]

38
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:47,607
You're not Lily.

39
00:01:47,690 --> 00:01:49,734
[instrumental theme music playing]

40
00:01:49,818 --> 00:01:53,321
Lily's my daughter. I have to save her.

41
00:01:53,822 --> 00:01:57,117
Lily's in danger. You have to help me.

42
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,828
-But, Mom…
-Help me. Let's look for Lily.

43
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:04,415
I have to get out of here.
I need to find Lily.

44
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:08,086
-But, Mom…
-I'm begging you. Help me.

45
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:14,134
[sobbing] Help me find Lily.
I need to get out of here.

46
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:16,052
[sobbing uncontrollably]

47
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:26,396
Okay.

48
00:02:27,605 --> 00:02:28,898
I'll help you.

49
00:02:31,609 --> 00:02:35,822
I'll help you… I'll help you find Lily.

50
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:41,828
Thank you. Thank you very much.

51
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:47,876
[instrumental theme music playing]

52
00:02:47,959 --> 00:02:48,877
[Camia sniffles]

53
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:51,921
Lily.

54
00:02:52,797 --> 00:02:55,091
[breathing heavily]

55
00:02:55,174 --> 00:02:56,593
[Camia] Lily.

56
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:04,976
Lily, my baby, wherever you are…

57
00:03:06,644 --> 00:03:08,021
please know I love you so much.

58
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:13,109
[sniffles]

59
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:14,736
I love you so much.

60
00:03:22,201 --> 00:03:23,453
You know what?

61
00:03:27,332 --> 00:03:29,292
Wherever Lily might be right now…

62
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:36,132
I'm sure she misses you a lot.

63
00:03:38,009 --> 00:03:42,555
I'm sure Lily loves you so much.
And she wants to be with you.

64
00:03:46,684 --> 00:03:51,356
That's why I'll help you find Lily.

65
00:03:57,528 --> 00:04:00,281
But if you really want to see Lily again…

66
00:04:02,075 --> 00:04:03,993
then we need to get out of here.

67
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:10,124
We need to leave this house
if you still want to see Lily.

68
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:14,963
Yes. Yes, let's leave.

69
00:04:16,631 --> 00:04:19,217
I want to hug my daughter again.

70
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:27,976
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]

71
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:34,274
<i>♪ Let her cry, for she's a lady… ♪</i>

72
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:35,525
[Camia] Lily…

73
00:04:35,608 --> 00:04:38,528
<i>♪ Let her dream ♪</i>

74
00:04:38,611 --> 00:04:40,321
<i>♪ For she's a child ♪</i>

75
00:04:40,405 --> 00:04:41,781
<i>♪ She's a child ♪</i>

76
00:04:41,864 --> 00:04:48,830
<i>♪ Let the rain fall down upon her ♪</i>

77
00:04:48,913 --> 00:04:55,920
<i>♪ She's a free and gentle flower</i>
<i>Growing wild ♪</i>

78
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:59,007
I won't rest easy
until I get to talk to Ivy.

79
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:02,135
I want to hear the truth
straight from her.

80
00:05:02,218 --> 00:05:08,057
But Ivy's missing.
What if she's hiding from you?

81
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:13,021
Or maybe she found out that
you already know her secret.

82
00:05:14,439 --> 00:05:17,233
Diego, Miss Aguas is a good person.

83
00:05:17,358 --> 00:05:18,901
But considering the fact

84
00:05:18,985 --> 00:05:21,446
that she kept all these things from you,

85
00:05:21,612 --> 00:05:25,116
I have a feeling she's up to
something against your family.

86
00:05:26,159 --> 00:05:28,453
[Pandoy] What will you do now, Diego?

87
00:05:28,536 --> 00:05:31,331
Will you warn your family
against Miss Aguas?

88
00:05:32,999 --> 00:05:34,834
-[tense music playing]
-[sighs]

89
00:05:35,126 --> 00:05:36,753
[phone ringing]

90
00:05:41,257 --> 00:05:42,800
-Hello?
-Sir Diego.

91
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:44,802
Your grandfather is asking for you.

92
00:05:44,969 --> 00:05:47,138
[foreboding music playing]

93
00:05:56,147 --> 00:05:57,398
[screaming]

94
00:05:57,482 --> 00:05:59,025
Help!

95
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:02,487
[cries] Nanny, help! Ouch!

96
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:08,201
My eyes! Ouch! Nanny!

97
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:11,079
Arnaldo! The water's been cut off!

98
00:06:11,287 --> 00:06:15,666
Oh, it hurts! Nanny! Arnaldo!

99
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,418
Ouch! It hurts!

100
00:06:17,502 --> 00:06:18,753
[crying]

101
00:06:21,881 --> 00:06:22,924
Ouch.

102
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:27,887
Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!
I can't see! I can't see! Ow!

103
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:31,182
-[Arnaldo] Mom?
-Arnaldo!

104
00:06:31,265 --> 00:06:33,017
Hey, what happened here? What's wrong?

105
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:34,227
[crying]

106
00:06:34,769 --> 00:06:36,896
The water's been cut off!

107
00:06:38,773 --> 00:06:40,316
-Arnaldo!
-Why did this happen?

108
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:42,610
It's been a long time
since this house was lived in.

109
00:06:42,693 --> 00:06:43,945
The pipes are broken.

110
00:06:44,028 --> 00:06:45,154
-[crying]
-[phone ringing]

111
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:46,948
[Emilia] Your grandfather
is maltreating me.

112
00:06:47,031 --> 00:06:49,242
-I hate him!
-[ringing continues]

113
00:06:50,451 --> 00:06:53,162
Can you please turn that off?!
It's so noisy!

114
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,998
I'm sorry, Governor. My mother's calling.

115
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:58,417
I don't care if your mother's calling!

116
00:06:58,584 --> 00:07:00,002
[crying]

117
00:07:00,086 --> 00:07:01,754
Arnaldo!

118
00:07:02,004 --> 00:07:06,592
[crying] No water. My eyes hurt.

119
00:07:07,051 --> 00:07:09,846
And you, Raul, why aren't you helping?!

120
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:12,807
If you think Papa will only punish me,

121
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:15,935
then you're wrong!
He wants us both to rot in hell!

122
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:19,063
My life here is so miserable.

123
00:07:19,147 --> 00:07:21,315
Look at the house. It's so old!

124
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:23,025
-Arnaldo, do something.
-Yes. Yes.

125
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:24,318
I'll do something about it.

126
00:07:24,902 --> 00:07:25,987
[Emilia] Thank you.

127
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:28,948
[phone ringing]

128
00:07:30,199 --> 00:07:32,743
Nanny, didn't I tell you not to call me?

129
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:35,997
I'm sorry, Jepoy. But it's an emergency.

130
00:07:36,372 --> 00:07:39,333
Diego found out that Ivy is Lily.

131
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:40,877
[suspenseful music playing]

132
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:43,671
What if he tells the Ardientes?

133
00:07:45,214 --> 00:07:46,257
But, how…

134
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:53,097
Nanny, Diego's here.

135
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:54,724
Stop him!

136
00:07:55,016 --> 00:07:57,185
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[breathes heavily]

137
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:13,618
Have a drink.

138
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:15,536
Thank you.

139
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:18,289
[soft music playing]

140
00:08:20,458 --> 00:08:22,376
Thank you for helping me.

141
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:26,005
Don't worry. We'll get out of here.

142
00:08:29,967 --> 00:08:30,968
You know what?

143
00:08:31,302 --> 00:08:32,887
You look beautiful when you smile.

144
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:38,476
You look like my daughter, Lily.

145
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:44,232
You're very beautiful too.

146
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:49,278
Uh…

147
00:08:50,446 --> 00:08:54,367
Can I call you "Mom"?

148
00:08:56,327 --> 00:08:59,413
I just really miss my mom.

149
00:09:02,124 --> 00:09:03,251
Okay.

150
00:09:06,254 --> 00:09:07,505
Thank you, Mom.

151
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:16,013
[foreboding music playing]

152
00:09:21,018 --> 00:09:22,103
Grandpa.

153
00:09:22,186 --> 00:09:26,023
Oh. Diego, my grandson. Come, sit down.

154
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:38,369
Grandpa, what do you want from me?

155
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:40,788
Um…

156
00:09:41,789 --> 00:09:44,292
Actually, it's not you whom I need.

157
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:45,876
It's…

158
00:09:46,544 --> 00:09:48,796
Miss Ivy Aguas.

159
00:09:51,132 --> 00:09:57,638
I have some unfinished business
with that woman.

160
00:09:59,015 --> 00:10:05,688
But unfortunately,
she just vanished into thin air.

161
00:10:08,190 --> 00:10:14,322
And as far as I know,
when a person is in hiding…

162
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:19,285
it means they're concealing some secrets.

163
00:10:19,535 --> 00:10:21,370
[tense music playing]

164
00:10:35,134 --> 00:10:39,055
You must be tired. Come, let's eat.

165
00:10:46,228 --> 00:10:47,146
[knife clinks]

166
00:10:47,229 --> 00:10:48,731
-Here.
-Thank you, Mom.

167
00:10:52,943 --> 00:10:54,028
You know…

168
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:58,324
You remind me of my husband, Dante.

169
00:10:59,158 --> 00:11:00,534
He was very hardworking.

170
00:11:00,826 --> 00:11:04,413
Even if he was tired,
he'd help me with the chores.

171
00:11:06,582 --> 00:11:08,376
Lily really took after him.

172
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:12,129
Hold on.

173
00:11:13,589 --> 00:11:15,716
Lily had a best friend.

174
00:11:17,593 --> 00:11:18,636
Diego.

175
00:11:19,887 --> 00:11:22,014
Could Lily be with him?

176
00:11:23,265 --> 00:11:25,810
You remember Diego?

177
00:11:26,811 --> 00:11:28,729
You're always with Miss Aguas, right?

178
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,523
Um…

179
00:11:31,190 --> 00:11:32,274
Oh.

180
00:11:32,566 --> 00:11:36,862
You helped the farmers together.

181
00:11:38,697 --> 00:11:45,663
And I heard that you've become
quite attached to this woman.

182
00:11:45,746 --> 00:11:47,206
[dark dramatic music playing]

183
00:11:47,289 --> 00:11:48,124
What?

184
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:51,043
Where did you hear that?

185
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:53,045
[chuckling]

186
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:56,465
Oh, Diego.

187
00:11:56,882 --> 00:12:03,139
There's not a thing in my town
that I don't know about.

188
00:12:05,641 --> 00:12:06,684
[Camia] Yes.

189
00:12:07,601 --> 00:12:09,603
He was my daughter's best friend.

190
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:13,691
He'll help us. Let's ask him for help.

191
00:12:13,774 --> 00:12:16,861
I'm sure he'll help us get out of here.

192
00:12:18,696 --> 00:12:19,780
That's too risky.

193
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:21,574
We're not sure if…

194
00:12:23,534 --> 00:12:25,411
if we can trust him.

195
00:12:29,999 --> 00:12:31,750
Why do you say that?

196
00:12:31,834 --> 00:12:35,963
I'm sure… Diego would help Lily.

197
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:39,633
[Julio] Why?

198
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:44,221
Will you go against your own family

199
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:45,431
for that woman?

200
00:12:47,725 --> 00:12:48,809
Don't, Diego.

201
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:53,439
Because that will make you a traitor.

202
00:12:55,691 --> 00:13:01,614
Now, where is Miss Aguas, and…

203
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:05,868
what do you know about her?

204
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:11,040
What?!

205
00:13:11,582 --> 00:13:12,875
Answer me!

206
00:13:15,211 --> 00:13:16,962
I'll ask again.

207
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:21,967
Where is Miss Aguas?

208
00:13:24,178 --> 00:13:26,972
Where is she hiding?

209
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:32,311
Ivy is a good person, Grandpa.

210
00:13:32,853 --> 00:13:34,313
She helped the farmers

211
00:13:34,396 --> 00:13:36,941
get what the politicians
long promised them.

212
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:39,485
And even if I knew where Ivy was…

213
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:41,779
I wouldn't tell you.

214
00:13:42,321 --> 00:13:43,239
[scoffs]

215
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:47,993
You idiot!

216
00:13:48,244 --> 00:13:50,579
[suspenseful music playing]

217
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:54,458
Go ahead, Grandpa. Try me.

218
00:13:56,418 --> 00:13:58,754
I'm not the same kid you used to abuse.

219
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:01,340
You can't scare me.

220
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:14,979
[Julio sets down crutch]

221
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:18,232
Who do you think you are?

222
00:14:19,775 --> 00:14:21,235
I raised you!

223
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:24,446
I fed you and sent you to school.

224
00:14:25,322 --> 00:14:31,203
Don't ever think that you can
go against this family.

225
00:14:31,662 --> 00:14:33,622
Even though you're my grandson,

226
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:37,251
I won't think twice about killing you!

227
00:14:37,501 --> 00:14:38,919
[suspenseful music playing]

228
00:14:39,211 --> 00:14:40,754
Grandpa, I'm not scared of you.

229
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:44,800
I'm just fighting for what's right.

230
00:14:48,345 --> 00:14:52,349
I'm ashamed to even call you an Ardiente.

231
00:14:54,727 --> 00:14:57,104
I don't want to see your face.

232
00:15:00,816 --> 00:15:03,319
Get out of my sight! Leave!

233
00:15:03,402 --> 00:15:05,029
[suspenseful music playing]

234
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:10,242
[Julio breathing heavily]

235
00:15:15,414 --> 00:15:16,999
[tense music playing]

236
00:15:19,752 --> 00:15:20,878
[sighs]

237
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:29,762
Mom, for now, we can't
be sure of anything.

238
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:38,020
Nowadays, we don't know
whom we should trust,

239
00:15:38,687 --> 00:15:40,648
or whom we can trust.

240
00:15:44,568 --> 00:15:45,819
You and me.

241
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:50,866
Right now, we only have each other.

242
00:15:51,116 --> 00:15:52,534
Just you and me.

243
00:15:56,747 --> 00:15:58,040
You're a brave woman.

244
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:02,294
But I can feel you're a good person too.

245
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:07,007
I'm sure your parents are so proud of you.

246
00:16:17,142 --> 00:16:18,352
Thank you.

247
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:27,236
It's good to know that…

248
00:16:27,611 --> 00:16:31,657
you hid Ivy's true identity
from your grandfather.

249
00:16:32,491 --> 00:16:34,243
Uncle, I won't reveal Ivy's secret.

250
00:16:35,202 --> 00:16:38,956
I know she has a reason
for doing what she's doing.

251
00:16:39,248 --> 00:16:41,542
But you need to talk to her.

252
00:16:41,792 --> 00:16:45,295
Fooling the Ardientes
like that is no joke.

253
00:16:45,796 --> 00:16:47,464
With how cruel your family is,

254
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:51,260
her days are numbered
if they learn her secret.

255
00:16:53,512 --> 00:16:56,390
I'll sort all this out. I'll look for Ivy.

256
00:16:56,849 --> 00:16:58,767
How will you find her?

257
00:16:58,892 --> 00:17:02,521
Where will you start?
Who knows where she is?

258
00:17:02,604 --> 00:17:04,106
[suspenseful music playing]

259
00:17:15,325 --> 00:17:17,703
[foreboding music playing]

260
00:17:38,432 --> 00:17:39,600
Where are you going?

261
00:17:41,643 --> 00:17:44,104
Where are you going?!
You're going to leave me?!

262
00:17:44,563 --> 00:17:47,649
You bastard. You haven't changed at all!

263
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:50,402
What's this?! Are you leaving me?!

264
00:17:50,486 --> 00:17:53,030
You're going to your mistress again?!

265
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,948
Huh?! Answer me!

266
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:56,200
[unzips bag]

267
00:17:57,785 --> 00:17:59,703
This is mine. This is mine!

268
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,538
You gave this to me
as a gift last Valentine's Day!

269
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:04,666
Now you're giving it
to your mistress?! You bastard!

270
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:06,835
When will you stop cheating on me?!

271
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:09,630
Why? Are you so sick of me?

272
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:12,424
So you run off
with that loose woman of yours?!

273
00:18:12,883 --> 00:18:16,136
Go on, do it. I'll burn her to ashes!

274
00:18:17,846 --> 00:18:20,015
Give me that. All you do is talk.

275
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:21,642
-You're not leaving.
-Get out of the way!

276
00:18:21,725 --> 00:18:24,686
No! I won't let you leave, Raul!

277
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:25,979
-I said--
-Don't try me!

278
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:28,232
-Step aside!
-Guards! Guards!

279
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:32,820
Deal with this man.

280
00:18:33,153 --> 00:18:36,532
Now go ahead and try to leave.

281
00:18:37,783 --> 00:18:40,702
And don't you ever try
giving this to your mistress!

282
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:41,912
This is mine!

283
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:44,373
You take care of him!

284
00:18:44,998 --> 00:18:46,542
[suspenseful music playing]

285
00:18:47,292 --> 00:18:48,418
[door slams]

286
00:18:56,301 --> 00:18:58,804
[tense music playing]

287
00:19:06,061 --> 00:19:07,771
[phone ringing]

288
00:19:09,106 --> 00:19:10,315
Hello, Nanny.

289
00:19:11,608 --> 00:19:12,609
Yes.

290
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:16,738
I'm at the place where I last
saw Ivy before she went missing.

291
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:20,284
Maybe I'll find clues
that'll point me to her.

292
00:19:22,411 --> 00:19:25,330
Yes, Nanny. Don't worry. I'll be careful.

293
00:19:27,791 --> 00:19:29,793
[tense music playing]

294
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:36,967
What are you doing here?

295
00:19:41,138 --> 00:19:42,222
[Emilia] It's so hot.

296
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:51,273
[foreboding music playing]

297
00:19:57,154 --> 00:19:58,488
[Julio] Good morning, Emilia.

298
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:00,365
[Emilia] Good morning, Papa.

299
00:20:00,949 --> 00:20:04,786
Stop. You don't have to act nice.

300
00:20:06,079 --> 00:20:07,623
There aren't any cameras here.

301
00:20:08,665 --> 00:20:13,670
I just came to know
how your first night here was.

302
00:20:14,922 --> 00:20:17,257
I heard you and your husband

303
00:20:17,507 --> 00:20:21,178
were fighting like cats
and dogs again last night.

304
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:23,430
That was nothing, Papa.

305
00:20:23,972 --> 00:20:27,684
It's normal for couples
to have petty lovers' quarrels.

306
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:28,810
[chuckles]

307
00:20:29,686 --> 00:20:31,188
"Petty lovers' quarrel."

308
00:20:31,563 --> 00:20:32,981
The quarrel was petty, but…

309
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:35,776
the reason behind it was not.

310
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:42,741
I'm warning you, Emilia,
you're pulling each other down.

311
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:48,664
And I won't let you drag
my name down with you.

312
00:20:49,665 --> 00:20:52,251
You're a failure as a wife.

313
00:20:53,919 --> 00:20:56,672
A failure as a mother.

314
00:20:58,382 --> 00:21:00,092
You're a failure as a governor.

315
00:21:00,592 --> 00:21:04,888
Most of all,
you're a failure as a daughter.

316
00:21:06,598 --> 00:21:09,101
[gloomy music playing]

317
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:17,859
I am not a failure, Papa.
I am not a failure.

318
00:21:29,788 --> 00:21:34,668
I… I'm going to a farm.
What are you doing here?

319
00:21:35,043 --> 00:21:36,712
This is where I last saw Ivy Aguas.

320
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:40,799
Grandpa asked me to find her.
Are you looking for her too?

321
00:21:41,591 --> 00:21:45,679
What? Why would I look for Ivy?
I don't need anything from her.

322
00:21:46,972 --> 00:21:48,015
[exhales sharply]

323
00:21:48,098 --> 00:21:49,057
Be careful.

324
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,811
If I find out you're betraying us again…

325
00:21:54,313 --> 00:21:55,856
I'll forget you're my brother.

326
00:21:58,025 --> 00:22:00,360
[tense music playing]

327
00:22:43,737 --> 00:22:45,072
-That's enough.
-No, Mom.

328
00:22:45,155 --> 00:22:46,531
We need to get out of here…

329
00:22:47,824 --> 00:22:49,701
before that bastard Raul comes back again.

330
00:22:53,789 --> 00:22:55,499
-That's enough. That's enough.
-No, Mom.

331
00:22:55,582 --> 00:22:57,167
-We need to get out of here!
-That's enough.

332
00:22:57,250 --> 00:22:58,335
That's enough.

333
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:04,633
[soft piano music playing]

334
00:23:22,859 --> 00:23:24,986
Mom, I'm sorry if I woke you up.

335
00:23:40,961 --> 00:23:43,171
[mysterious music playing]

336
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:58,186
Hello? Anyone here?

337
00:23:59,437 --> 00:24:00,438
Yes?

338
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:03,108
-Uh… Good afternoon.
-Good afternoon to you too.

339
00:24:03,191 --> 00:24:04,985
The owner of that car…

340
00:24:06,486 --> 00:24:07,654
where is she?

341
00:24:08,572 --> 00:24:11,867
Mister, I'm her friend.
Her name's Ivy Aguas.

342
00:24:12,367 --> 00:24:15,954
She's been missing for a few days now,
so please tell me where she is.

343
00:24:16,037 --> 00:24:18,707
Uh… She went to the old Torillo house

344
00:24:18,790 --> 00:24:20,125
here in San Ildefonso.

345
00:24:21,668 --> 00:24:23,086
Raul Torillo?

346
00:24:23,587 --> 00:24:24,379
Yes.

347
00:24:25,213 --> 00:24:26,548
Why did she go there?

348
00:24:26,631 --> 00:24:27,674
I don't know.

349
00:24:27,757 --> 00:24:31,553
I've not seen her again
since she left her car here.

350
00:24:34,973 --> 00:24:35,932
Thank you.

351
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:46,860
[instrumental theme music playing]

352
00:24:49,029 --> 00:24:50,071
You know…

353
00:24:51,531 --> 00:24:52,657
I'm a teacher.

354
00:24:55,660 --> 00:24:58,788
You can't force things to happen.

355
00:24:59,873 --> 00:25:02,042
You need patience.

356
00:25:03,043 --> 00:25:08,673
You need to think things through
before you act.

357
00:25:11,218 --> 00:25:13,803
[instrumental theme music playing]

358
00:25:34,115 --> 00:25:35,533
[line ringing]

359
00:25:36,826 --> 00:25:40,038
[loudly] Nanny, Uncle.
I'm heading to San Ildefonso.

360
00:25:40,789 --> 00:25:42,082
<i>I heard…</i>

361
00:25:42,290 --> 00:25:44,501
that Ivy went to Dad's old house there.

362
00:25:45,001 --> 00:25:49,047
What's Miss Aguas doing there?
What is she doing with your dad?

363
00:25:49,381 --> 00:25:51,007
I don't know.

364
00:25:51,883 --> 00:25:54,719
They both left Arnaldo's party
at the same time.

365
00:25:55,428 --> 00:25:56,304
<i>But I'm not sure.</i>

366
00:25:56,388 --> 00:25:57,389
Could've been a coincidence.

367
00:25:58,056 --> 00:26:02,686
Could Raul know about Miss Aguas' secret?

368
00:26:04,229 --> 00:26:05,939
That's what I need to find out.

369
00:26:06,439 --> 00:26:07,565
Do you know how to get there?

370
00:26:07,649 --> 00:26:12,237
No, Uncle. Dad never took us there before.

371
00:26:12,821 --> 00:26:13,863
<i>But…</i>

372
00:26:14,114 --> 00:26:15,824
I'll just ask around for directions.

373
00:26:16,157 --> 00:26:17,784
Take care, Diego.

374
00:26:18,201 --> 00:26:19,494
Don't worry about me.

375
00:26:19,577 --> 00:26:21,204
[tense music playing]

376
00:26:26,501 --> 00:26:28,670
[dark piano music playing]

377
00:26:32,549 --> 00:26:33,591
[Jepoy] Hi, Governor.

378
00:26:34,259 --> 00:26:35,844
I'm sorry, I thought no one was here.

379
00:26:36,219 --> 00:26:39,723
Madrigal? They call you "Madrigal," right?

380
00:26:40,598 --> 00:26:41,641
Yes, Governor.

381
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:44,936
Come join me for a drink.

382
00:26:45,770 --> 00:26:46,563
I'm sorry, Governor.

383
00:26:46,646 --> 00:26:48,231
We aren't allowed to drink
during working hours.

384
00:26:48,982 --> 00:26:50,025
Says who?

385
00:26:50,817 --> 00:26:51,860
My boss.

386
00:26:53,611 --> 00:26:55,322
Well, who are you guarding right now?

387
00:26:55,405 --> 00:26:56,614
Me, right?

388
00:26:57,115 --> 00:26:59,409
So, that means I'm your boss.

389
00:26:59,909 --> 00:27:01,661
Sit and join me for a drink.

390
00:27:19,095 --> 00:27:20,180
[ice clinks in glass]

391
00:27:23,725 --> 00:27:24,768
-Grandpa.
-Oh.

392
00:27:24,893 --> 00:27:28,980
Arnaldo, sit down. Join me for some tea.

393
00:27:32,567 --> 00:27:36,029
It looks like you're home early.

394
00:27:36,571 --> 00:27:39,616
Uh, Grandpa, I wasn't able
to get any news on Miss Aguas.

395
00:27:40,116 --> 00:27:41,785
I went to the last place

396
00:27:41,868 --> 00:27:43,787
where I saw her,
but I still didn't get anything.

397
00:27:44,788 --> 00:27:46,790
And you just gave up?

398
00:27:50,126 --> 00:27:54,089
You know, Arnaldo, I don't remember…

399
00:27:54,589 --> 00:27:56,883
teaching you to be weak.

400
00:27:58,885 --> 00:28:00,512
No, Grandpa. I'm not giving up.

401
00:28:00,804 --> 00:28:03,264
I came home early to check
on Mama at the guesthouse.

402
00:28:04,265 --> 00:28:06,601
Exactly what I'm talking about.

403
00:28:08,728 --> 00:28:11,523
Your mother is pulling you down.

404
00:28:11,648 --> 00:28:13,817
[dark dramatic music playing]

405
00:28:13,900 --> 00:28:17,904
A hunter who shows his weaknesses…

406
00:28:18,530 --> 00:28:20,865
soon becomes the hunted.

407
00:28:22,784 --> 00:28:26,788
So, don't be weak like your parents.

408
00:28:41,344 --> 00:28:44,431
Madrigal, how long have you
been working for us?

409
00:28:44,806 --> 00:28:46,141
Five or six years?

410
00:28:46,808 --> 00:28:48,768
That sounds about right, Governor.

411
00:28:49,185 --> 00:28:52,480
So that means, you know me.

412
00:28:53,940 --> 00:28:56,067
And you know my husband very well.

413
00:28:56,568 --> 00:28:59,362
So, do you think my husband
is having an affair?

414
00:29:00,739 --> 00:29:01,740
I'm sorry, Governor.

415
00:29:02,157 --> 00:29:04,659
I have no right to interfere
with your married life.

416
00:29:06,077 --> 00:29:08,079
[dark piano music playing]

417
00:29:21,718 --> 00:29:24,512
Do you think I'm capable
of cheating on my husband?

418
00:29:27,432 --> 00:29:28,433
[sighs]

419
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:30,685
How I wish I could.

420
00:29:32,020 --> 00:29:34,606
But even if I do it in front of him…

421
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:38,359
the question is, would he even care?

422
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:43,865
Or would I end up getting hurt?

423
00:29:45,408 --> 00:29:50,205
You see, Madrigal, my husband's
had so many mistresses.

424
00:29:50,747 --> 00:29:54,334
But not one of them succeeded
in taking him from me.

425
00:29:55,293 --> 00:29:58,296
So, I'm thinking that this woman…

426
00:29:59,881 --> 00:30:03,468
is just one of those cheap mistresses…

427
00:30:04,969 --> 00:30:08,681
that I can easily wipe off
the face of the earth.

428
00:30:12,143 --> 00:30:14,604
[suspenseful music playing]

429
00:30:27,659 --> 00:30:29,285
[unsettling music playing]

430
00:30:35,959 --> 00:30:37,001
Mom?

431
00:30:39,462 --> 00:30:40,505
[lock clicks]

432
00:30:44,259 --> 00:30:45,927
[birds chirping]

433
00:31:10,994 --> 00:31:11,995
Mom?

434
00:31:12,787 --> 00:31:13,830
[knocking]

435
00:31:14,706 --> 00:31:16,040
Are you okay?

436
00:31:30,805 --> 00:31:31,931
Mom, what's wrong?

437
00:31:33,349 --> 00:31:35,810
Nothing. I just used the restroom.

438
00:31:46,195 --> 00:31:48,406
Uh… Come on. Get some rest.

439
00:32:03,254 --> 00:32:05,298
Sit there, Mom. I need to keep

440
00:32:05,381 --> 00:32:06,758
-tearing down the wall.
-[car engine starts]

441
00:32:08,676 --> 00:32:09,969
That sounds like a car.

442
00:32:19,979 --> 00:32:21,064
Diego?

443
00:32:23,650 --> 00:32:25,693
-Diego!
-[pounding on window]

444
00:32:26,235 --> 00:32:27,487
Diego!

445
00:32:28,655 --> 00:32:31,199
Diego, we're here! Diego!

446
00:32:33,743 --> 00:32:34,786
Diego!

447
00:32:36,704 --> 00:32:37,789
He already left.

448
00:32:39,207 --> 00:32:41,376
Mom, that was Diego. My childhood--

449
00:32:42,543 --> 00:32:43,962
Lily's childhood friend.

450
00:32:44,754 --> 00:32:46,130
Diego.

451
00:32:46,422 --> 00:32:47,423
Diego?

452
00:32:47,799 --> 00:32:48,800
Yes.

453
00:32:49,008 --> 00:32:50,718
He's Lily's childhood friend.

454
00:32:52,178 --> 00:32:57,809
Don't worry. They'll find a way
to get us out of this house.

455
00:32:59,060 --> 00:33:01,771
But how will they find us
in a place like this?

456
00:33:04,816 --> 00:33:05,900
I don't know.

457
00:33:06,609 --> 00:33:11,114
But I believe that they will
be able to find us.

458
00:33:11,698 --> 00:33:14,659
I'll save you. I'll find a way.

459
00:33:15,368 --> 00:33:16,577
I'll save you.

460
00:33:16,661 --> 00:33:19,622
[tense music playing]

461
00:33:28,464 --> 00:33:30,758
[foreboding music playing]

462
00:33:45,773 --> 00:33:48,026
Sir, this is all we got from the kitchen.

463
00:33:48,109 --> 00:33:49,736
Oh. Are you sure?

464
00:33:50,570 --> 00:33:53,865
You hid some of it, didn't you?

465
00:33:53,948 --> 00:33:54,907
[chuckles]

466
00:33:58,202 --> 00:33:59,495
Go ahead. Let's drink.

467
00:34:01,664 --> 00:34:03,249
What if the congressman sees us?

468
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:05,835
Oh, come on! You're already
holding your glasses.

469
00:34:05,918 --> 00:34:09,088
We used to do this before. Right?

470
00:34:10,381 --> 00:34:12,925
Look. Can you say no to this?
It's your favorite.

471
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:16,345
Right? Besides, we're the only ones here.

472
00:34:16,471 --> 00:34:18,139
No one will get mad at us. Come on.

473
00:34:18,222 --> 00:34:19,682
-[glasses clink]
-Bottoms up!

474
00:34:21,059 --> 00:34:24,771
I went to my dad's house,
but Ivy Aguas wasn't there.

475
00:34:24,979 --> 00:34:27,065
That house is empty most of the time, sir.

476
00:34:27,148 --> 00:34:29,901
I only saw Mr. Torillo
once or twice there.

477
00:34:30,193 --> 00:34:33,613
Maybe, this Ivy you're looking
for isn't here in San Ildefonso.

478
00:34:33,821 --> 00:34:35,823
Chief, her car was found here.

479
00:34:36,115 --> 00:34:38,493
She couldn't just disappear
all of a sudden.

480
00:34:38,701 --> 00:34:40,369
What if something bad happened to her?

481
00:34:40,995 --> 00:34:42,789
What should we do?

482
00:34:43,206 --> 00:34:45,083
Who is this Ivy Aguas anyway?

483
00:34:45,166 --> 00:34:47,043
And why is she here in San Ildefonso?

484
00:34:47,877 --> 00:34:50,421
Maybe, she… You know what I mean.

485
00:34:50,505 --> 00:34:51,756
[both laugh]

486
00:34:52,298 --> 00:34:55,676
Or maybe, she's Raul Torillo's mistress.

487
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:58,012
It's the talk of the town…

488
00:34:58,846 --> 00:35:00,431
that your dad is a womanizer.

489
00:35:01,349 --> 00:35:04,435
[cop Manansala] But don't worry.
We'll go to that house.

490
00:35:04,644 --> 00:35:06,979
We'll also tell our other officers

491
00:35:07,146 --> 00:35:09,482
to help you find Ivy Aguas.

492
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:12,443
Thank you.

493
00:35:18,074 --> 00:35:20,159
Let's have another drink. Hey!

494
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:21,994
Hey!

495
00:35:22,870 --> 00:35:23,871
Psst!

496
00:35:24,539 --> 00:35:25,706
Let's have another round.

497
00:35:27,792 --> 00:35:29,210
Hey. Gave up already?

498
00:35:30,294 --> 00:35:32,421
[sinister music playing]

499
00:35:39,762 --> 00:35:40,805
[car alarm chirps]

500
00:35:48,563 --> 00:35:49,730
[car engine starts]

501
00:36:00,658 --> 00:36:03,202
[Emilia] <i>I'll find out who</i>
<i>your mistress is, Raul.</i>

502
00:36:04,036 --> 00:36:05,246
<i>Then, you'll see.</i>

503
00:36:07,206 --> 00:36:08,457
Come with me.

504
00:36:30,062 --> 00:36:31,772
[vehicle approaching]

505
00:36:39,071 --> 00:36:40,323
Someone's coming.

506
00:36:52,501 --> 00:36:55,671
Mom, it's Raul. Raul's back.

507
00:36:59,550 --> 00:37:01,677
[suspenseful music playing]

508
00:37:01,969 --> 00:37:06,432
Mom, listen to me.
Raul can't know I'm here.

509
00:37:06,515 --> 00:37:08,559
He can't know you aren't alone.

510
00:37:08,643 --> 00:37:10,937
If he does, I'm sure he'll hurt you.

511
00:37:11,020 --> 00:37:12,313
He'll hurt us both.

512
00:37:15,358 --> 00:37:16,400
[car alarm chirps]

513
00:37:17,318 --> 00:37:18,611
Don't worry, Mom.

514
00:37:18,736 --> 00:37:21,656
I promise I'll find a way
to get us out of here…

515
00:37:22,198 --> 00:37:25,952
so we can find Lily, right?
We'll find Lily.

516
00:37:26,369 --> 00:37:27,286
Love?

517
00:37:27,370 --> 00:37:30,164
[foreboding music playing]

518
00:37:30,957 --> 00:37:32,208
Mom, I'll be hiding now.

519
00:37:32,291 --> 00:37:33,918
-[Raul] Jasmin?
-[Ivy] Don't tell him I'm here.

520
00:37:34,460 --> 00:37:36,087
Jasmin, I'm home.

521
00:37:42,176 --> 00:37:43,135
Love?

522
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:48,975
Love.

523
00:37:50,518 --> 00:37:52,687
[tense music playing]

524
00:37:55,064 --> 00:37:56,023
How are you?

525
00:37:56,357 --> 00:37:58,985
Did you eat well here? Huh?

526
00:37:59,527 --> 00:38:02,905
I'm sorry I couldn't come back sooner.

527
00:38:03,072 --> 00:38:06,158
I just had to settle everything
I had to settle,

528
00:38:06,325 --> 00:38:09,287
so we can live happily together,
without any problems,

529
00:38:09,370 --> 00:38:11,747
and with no one
bothering us anymore. Okay?

530
00:38:22,174 --> 00:38:24,468
[suspenseful music playing]

531
00:38:34,228 --> 00:38:36,063
[Raul] You're going to love
what I brought you.

532
00:38:37,773 --> 00:38:39,150
These are for you.

533
00:38:39,567 --> 00:38:41,110
This one, it's pretty.

534
00:38:41,193 --> 00:38:43,112
This will look really good on you.

535
00:38:43,279 --> 00:38:45,489
Some toiletries. We need these.

536
00:38:46,657 --> 00:38:49,493
Clothes. Here. I brought a lot.

537
00:38:49,869 --> 00:38:52,038
Let's see if it fits you.

538
00:38:55,207 --> 00:38:56,208
This looks…

539
00:38:56,542 --> 00:38:58,002
[laughing]

540
00:38:58,336 --> 00:38:59,879
So-- Sorry.

541
00:39:00,296 --> 00:39:03,632
I didn't know…
I think they're too big for you.

542
00:39:04,216 --> 00:39:08,387
Anyway, don't worry.
Next time I go to the store,

543
00:39:08,596 --> 00:39:10,806
I'll buy the right sizes, okay? I promise.

544
00:39:11,182 --> 00:39:12,600
I'll just return these clothes.

545
00:39:13,142 --> 00:39:16,187
But first, I'll sort our stuff out.

546
00:39:16,437 --> 00:39:17,938
I'll put these in your closet.

547
00:39:18,356 --> 00:39:20,608
[Raul] We don't want our stuff
scattered here, you know?

548
00:39:30,284 --> 00:39:31,285
What's wrong?

549
00:39:33,788 --> 00:39:34,872
What is it, love?

550
00:39:35,539 --> 00:39:36,665
I'm hungry.

551
00:39:42,963 --> 00:39:44,006
[bag thuds]

552
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:47,635
Did you just say you're hungry?

553
00:39:48,761 --> 00:39:50,054
You can talk now?

554
00:39:56,227 --> 00:39:57,311
Thank goodness.

555
00:39:58,729 --> 00:40:02,483
Love, you don't know how happy
you made me today.

556
00:40:02,942 --> 00:40:05,694
I guess I should buy us some food first.

557
00:40:05,778 --> 00:40:08,823
Then, we'll celebrate, okay?

558
00:40:09,782 --> 00:40:12,243
I love you so much. I won't be long.

559
00:40:13,369 --> 00:40:14,412
Raul…

560
00:40:18,958 --> 00:40:20,126
Come back, okay?

561
00:40:21,794 --> 00:40:23,712
I promise. I'll be back.

562
00:40:24,964 --> 00:40:27,425
[suspenseful music playing]

563
00:40:36,851 --> 00:40:38,978
[suspenseful music playing]

564
00:41:03,502 --> 00:41:04,545
Mom.

565
00:41:05,546 --> 00:41:08,674
We have to leave
before that bastard comes back.

566
00:41:09,091 --> 00:41:10,134
But how?

567
00:41:13,304 --> 00:41:16,765
[suspenseful music playing]

568
00:41:25,816 --> 00:41:28,611
Santos. Do it now.

569
00:41:42,333 --> 00:41:46,629
You chose the wrong man to flirt with.

570
00:41:46,962 --> 00:41:49,632
[suspenseful dramatic music playing]

571
00:42:02,228 --> 00:42:03,229
It's done, Governor.

572
00:42:03,354 --> 00:42:06,774
You can go now, Santos.
Leave the keys with me.

573
00:42:06,857 --> 00:42:07,858
Here.

574
00:42:08,817 --> 00:42:09,777
Fifty thousand.

575
00:42:10,152 --> 00:42:12,112
-Like what we agreed on.
-Thank you. Thank you, ma'am.

576
00:42:13,656 --> 00:42:15,783
[suspenseful music playing]

577
00:42:26,377 --> 00:42:28,921
[Emilia humming]

578
00:42:39,682 --> 00:42:41,892
[suspenseful music playing]

579
00:42:47,106 --> 00:42:49,024
[laughing]

580
00:42:50,818 --> 00:42:53,487
One great move, Emilia.

581
00:42:54,572 --> 00:42:55,614
Good job.

582
00:43:05,499 --> 00:43:08,043
[suspenseful music playing]

583
00:43:08,127 --> 00:43:09,503
[fire crackling]

584
00:43:19,722 --> 00:43:23,475
[laughing maniacally]

585
00:43:51,879 --> 00:43:54,340
[Camia] Fire! Fire!

586
00:43:54,423 --> 00:43:57,551
[laughing]

587
00:44:01,639 --> 00:44:03,349
-[Camia] Fire!
-[Ivy] Mom.

588
00:44:04,183 --> 00:44:05,476
[Camia] Fire!

589
00:44:06,518 --> 00:44:07,686
Fire!

590
00:44:08,771 --> 00:44:10,356
[breathing heavily]

591
00:44:13,150 --> 00:44:14,985
[Camia coughing]

592
00:44:15,861 --> 00:44:16,945
[Ivy] Mom!

593
00:44:19,114 --> 00:44:20,282
Mom, put this on.

594
00:44:21,075 --> 00:44:22,201
[coughing]

595
00:44:22,785 --> 00:44:24,036
[fire whooshing]

596
00:44:30,584 --> 00:44:31,669
[laughing]

597
00:44:32,127 --> 00:44:33,462
[fire whooshing]

598
00:44:34,296 --> 00:44:36,256
[coughing]

599
00:44:36,340 --> 00:44:37,383
[Ivy] Wait here.

600
00:44:38,509 --> 00:44:39,635
[coughing]

601
00:44:40,594 --> 00:44:41,720
[water running]

602
00:44:45,474 --> 00:44:46,642
Here, Mom.

603
00:44:50,771 --> 00:44:53,232
[both coughing]

604
00:44:54,149 --> 00:44:55,234
Hold on, Mom.

605
00:45:05,577 --> 00:45:08,580
[Camia screams] We're going to die here!

606
00:45:08,664 --> 00:45:09,832
[Ivy] No, we're not!

607
00:45:10,040 --> 00:45:11,417
[Camia] We're going to die!

608
00:45:11,500 --> 00:45:13,377
No, Mom! I'll get us out of here!

609
00:45:13,794 --> 00:45:15,879
[both coughing]

610
00:45:19,758 --> 00:45:21,260
[fire whooshing]

611
00:45:21,343 --> 00:45:25,180
-[laughing maniacally]
-[pounding on wall continues]

612
00:45:38,944 --> 00:45:41,572
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[fire whooshing]

613
00:45:44,741 --> 00:45:45,868
[wood clatters]

614
00:45:52,499 --> 00:45:53,750
[coughing]

615
00:45:55,377 --> 00:45:56,879
[Ivy] Careful, Mom.

616
00:45:59,006 --> 00:46:00,340
Poor girl.

617
00:46:00,966 --> 00:46:02,092
[Ivy] Wait here, Mom.

618
00:46:02,176 --> 00:46:04,553
[Emilia] <i>Your poor mistress, Raul.</i>

619
00:46:05,637 --> 00:46:07,264
<i>Nothing will be left of her.</i>

620
00:46:08,140 --> 00:46:09,475
<i>Toasted to death.</i>

621
00:46:10,559 --> 00:46:11,602
[chuckles]

622
00:46:12,603 --> 00:46:17,024
Even her soul will burn.

623
00:46:17,566 --> 00:46:18,567
[coughing]

624
00:46:20,152 --> 00:46:21,236
[Ivy] Come here, Mom!

625
00:46:24,323 --> 00:46:25,991
-[thudding, clattering]
-[screaming]

626
00:46:27,868 --> 00:46:29,369
-Mom!
-[fire whooshing]

627
00:46:30,204 --> 00:46:33,248
[laughing]

628
00:46:33,332 --> 00:46:34,458
Mom!

629
00:46:36,126 --> 00:46:38,837
Mom, come here! Mom!

630
00:46:38,921 --> 00:46:41,465
[suspenseful music playing]

631
00:46:46,720 --> 00:46:48,555
<i>Hello, Raul? Come back here.</i>

632
00:46:48,639 --> 00:46:50,057
<i>I have a surprise for you.</i>

633
00:46:50,140 --> 00:46:51,975
<i>What are you talking about, Emilia?</i>

634
00:46:52,059 --> 00:46:53,018
<i>Where will I go back?</i>

635
00:46:53,101 --> 00:46:55,729
<i>Where else? To the house of your mistress.</i>

636
00:46:55,812 --> 00:46:58,315
<i>Jepoy, do you have any news on Ivy?</i>

637
00:46:58,398 --> 00:46:59,691
<i>My gut's telling me</i>

638
00:46:59,775 --> 00:47:00,859
<i>-that if I find Raul,</i>
<i>-Mom!</i>

639
00:47:00,943 --> 00:47:01,735
[Jepoy] <i>I'll find Ivy too.</i>

640
00:47:01,818 --> 00:47:03,320
-[Ivy] <i>Wait!</i>
-[Camia coughing]

641
00:47:05,072 --> 00:47:06,323
[Raul sobbing] <i>Jasmin!</i>

642
00:47:06,823 --> 00:47:08,575
-<i>I'm here.</i>
-[laughing]

643
00:47:08,992 --> 00:47:10,536
<i>This isn't over, Emilia!</i>

644
00:47:11,161 --> 00:47:13,330
[Emilia] <i>The easiest way</i>
<i>to get rid of your enemies</i>

645
00:47:13,413 --> 00:47:14,706
<i>is to kill them.</i>

646
00:47:14,790 --> 00:47:18,710
<i>Because once you do that,</i>
<i>that means you've won.</i>

647
00:47:19,419 --> 00:47:22,464
[theme music playing]
